B = [
('Tupperware','North America','1950s-70s','homeware','In the style of Tupperware, cheerful domestic order in translucent, slightly frosted plastic with a matte waxy finish. Soft rounded corners, plump friendly volumes and tight fitting lids with a small raised central dimple. Forms are designed to nest and stack into neat, tidy towers. Colours are optimistic mid-century kitchen hues of avocado green, harvest gold, tangerine, pale turquoise, pink, mustard and almond, used in bold flat single colours. No ornament beyond moulded rings and simple ribs. Bright, wholesome, practical, suburban and joyful.'),
('Lodge','North America','19th century-present','homeware','In the style of Lodge, heavy, plain, indestructible forms in cast iron with a rough pebbly matte surface. Thick walls, rounded utilitarian volumes, simple pouring lips, sturdy loop or bail handles and a hole for hanging, with no decoration beyond a few raised ridges and a cast mark. Colour is matte charcoal black with glossy dark brown seasoning, slightly rusty edges and worn patches. Rustic, honest, campfire and cabin warmth, made to last generations and look better with use.'),
('Nambu ironworks','East Asia','17th century-present','homeware','In the style of Nambu ironworks, weighty cast-iron forms with rounded, bulging bodies and a quiet, austere, wabi-sabi presence. Surfaces carry rows of small raised bumps like hailstones in a tight regular grid, or finely cast relief motifs of pine, cranes, blossoms and waves, sometimes with fine silver inlay. Finish is matte black, deep brown or rust. Small knob tops, curved swing handles of dark metal and short elegant spouts. Simple, heavy, contemplative and ceremonial.'),
('Arita porcelain','East Asia','17th-19th century','ceramics','In the style of Arita porcelain, refined thin white porcelain with a milky body, clear sparkling glaze and a great deal of generous empty space. Crisp cobalt blue painted decoration of landscapes, pines, bamboo, cranes and flowers sits in asymmetrical, minimalist compositions with delicate fluid brushstrokes. Enamelled versions add small touches of red, green, yellow and sky blue. Shapes are elegant and crisp, including faceted and lobed outlines. Airy, graceful, calm and exact, like quiet tea house tableware.'),
('Imari ware','East Asia','17th-19th century','ceramics','In the style of Imari ware, flamboyant, dense, sumptuous decoration that leaves little blank white. A rich palette of deep underglaze cobalt blue, fiery iron red and lavish gold, with sections or panels of chrysanthemums, peonies, phoenixes, fans, waves and brocade-like patterns packed side by side. Blue areas alternate with red and gilded floral scrolls. Shapes are lobed and scalloped with ornate rims. Glossy glaze, heavy ornament, opulent and festive like woven silk brocade.'),
('Satsuma ware','East Asia','19th century','ceramics','In the style of Satsuma ware, jewel-like, glowing surfaces of cream-ivory glaze with a fine network of crackle. Every area is covered in miniature, densely painted scenes with tiny figures, gardens, mountains and blossoms in vivid enamels of red, green and blue, enriched with lavish raised gold and bands of brocade pattern at borders. Elaborate sculpted handles and pierced details. Highly detailed, warm, glowing, precious and ornate, like an export-era cabinet treasure.'),
('Moser','Europe','1900s-30s','glass','In the style of Moser, luxurious Bohemian crystal with heavy cut and engraved decoration. Deep facets, fluting and columns, gold-gilded rims and enamelled gold frames, with etched floral and animal motifs such as stags, swans and acanthus leaves. Intense transparent coloured glass in alexandrite purple, emerald green, cobalt, ruby, amber and smoky topaz. Rich, jewelled, glowing in warm lamplight, blending Belle Epoque grandeur with Art Deco elegance.'),
('Tolix','Europe','1930s','furniture','In the style of Tolix, tough, thin, urban industrial design pressed from single sheets of steel. Simple tapered legs, rounded pressed curves, perforations used as the only pattern, and reinforced edges and feet. Stackable, repeatable, economical forms with a visibly utilitarian build. Finish is matte lacquer, powder-coat or galvanised raw zinc in red, dark green, yellow, black, grey and silver, with dents, scuffs and a worn patina. Factory canteen and cafe terrace character, honest and unfussy.'),
('Louis Poulsen','Europe','1920s-60s','lighting','In the style of Louis Poulsen, calm, sculptural Scandinavian lighting logic where the light source is hidden and glare is controlled. Layered concentric shades, curved overlapping discs or dozens of overlapping leaf-like plates form smooth symmetrical shapes. Materials are polished steel, chrome, brass, copper and white lacquer with soft warm reflections. Smooth, restrained, elegant and perfectly proportioned, giving a soft diffused glow across a table.'),
('Anglepoise','Europe','1930s','lighting','In the style of Anglepoise, technical, balanced and flexible engineering shown honestly. Slender jointed arms, exposed coiled springs, small pivots and a conical shade posed in mid-air like a drawing compass, resting on a heavy stepped round base. Enamel or powder-coated metal in cream, black, red, grey, racing green and polished chrome. Everything looks adjustable and functional, with a drawing office and workshop atmosphere, lean, precise and a little vintage.'),
('Moorcroft','Europe','1900s-30s','ceramics','In the style of Moorcroft, English art pottery with hand-painted designs outlined in raised slip lines like cloisonne. Lush stylised plants, flowers, fruit and toadstools in Art Nouveau rhythm fill the surface with flowing curves. Deep jewel-toned glazes of royal blue, forest green, burgundy, plum and gold, with rich flambe runs and a smooth, glossy, velvety depth. Rounded, generous shapes, luminous colour and a precious, collectable Edwardian handmade feel.'),
('Emma Bridgewater','Europe','1990s-present','ceramics','In the style of Emma Bridgewater, cheerful cottagey earthenware in cream glaze with hand-sponged spots, dots, hearts, stars and stripes in blue, red and green. Bold black hand-lettered mottoes and rustic farm animals in simple painterly forms. Chunky, rounded shapes with irregular painted edges and speckled glaze. Warm, homely, slightly wonky and full of friendly character, like a kitchen dresser on a Sunday morning.'),
('Portmeirion','Europe','1960s-70s','ceramics','In the style of Portmeirion, lush, abundant botanical decoration embossed and printed on cream or white ground. Naturalistic flowers, ferns, fruit, butterflies and bees are crowded with leaves and vines in the manner of a Victorian botanical print book. Rich colours of burgundy, fern green, gold and cobalt blue. Chunky forms, scalloped and wide-rimmed edges and relief texture beneath the print. Cottage garden, apothecary, cosy and plentiful.'),
('Rosenthal','Europe','1950s-70s','ceramics','In the style of Rosenthal, sleek modern porcelain in smooth, pure white, with clean silhouettes, rounded cylinders, geometric ribs and sculptural relief. Thin gold or platinum rims and abstract hand-painted or printed patterns in black, cobalt, orange and brown, with bold stripes, pastel bands and playful 1970s psychedelic swirls. Crisp, glossy, translucent and elegant yet relaxed, a modernist gallery feel.'),
('Lomonosov Porcelain','Russia and Eastern Europe','1920s','ceramics','In the style of Lomonosov Porcelain, thin white porcelain used as a canvas for striking graphic energy. Geometric abstract shapes in flat red, black and white, bold angular lettering, stars, factories and stylised figures in the manner of revolutionary agitprop. Also a classic cobalt net pattern with gilded cell edges and small white relief bumps. Flat bold colour, dynamic diagonal compositions, a stern idealistic mood and a historical museum feel.'),
('Gzhel','Russia and Eastern Europe','17th century-present','ceramics','In the style of Gzhel, folk ceramics painted entirely in cobalt blue on bright white glaze. Brushstrokes shade fluidly from deep ink to pale sky blue, forming flowing flowers, leaves, scrolls, dots and drops that wrap around the form. Glossy smooth surfaces, a clean blue and white contrast, rounded plump forms and a joyful, fresh, handmade charm. Decoration is hand-brushed with confident single strokes, leaving plenty of bright white ground around each motif.'),
('Khokhloma','Russia and Eastern Europe','17th century-present','woodwork','In the style of Khokhloma, glowing gold-like swirling patterns painted on black or deep red lacquer. Curling vines, rowan berries, strawberries, leaves and flowers in red, black, gold and green flow in rhythmic curves across glossy varnished turned wood. A shiny golden-yellow undertone shows through from oven-hardened varnish. Rich, warm, curvilinear, festive and fairy-tale peasant treasure. Ornament is hand-brushed in confident repeating curls, evenly spread over the whole surface with little empty ground.'),
('Kutahya and Iznik ceramics','Middle East','16th-18th century','ceramics','In the style of Kutahya and Iznik ceramics, intense colour painted under crystal-clear glaze, with cobalt blue, turquoise, sage green, tomato red and white. Symmetrical, flowing patterns of tulips, carnations, hyacinths, rosebuds, long saw-edged leaves and curling arabesques repeat across surfaces, with radiating floral rosettes and tile-like repetition. Glossy, bright, crisp and elegant, evoking mosque walls and bazaars. Colour areas are crisp and flat, with fine dark outlines and bright white ground showing between motifs.'),
('Talavera de Puebla','Latin America','17th century-present','ceramics','In the style of Talavera de Puebla, thick creamy white glossy tin glaze painted by hand in cobalt blue, yellow, green, orange and black. Flowers, birds, vines, geometric borders and Moorish-inspired arabesques are laid down in bold brushwork, with slightly uneven edges, drips and pooling glaze. Rustic, festive, joyful, like a sunlit courtyard and hacienda kitchen. Colours stay bright and flat, edged with a thin dark outline, with white ground left between motifs.'),
('Royal Selangor','Southeast Asia','1900s-present','homeware','In the style of Royal Selangor, polished silvery grey pewter with a soft lustrous gleam and either smooth or hammered finish. Heavy-bottomed, rounded forms with simple handles, sometimes mixed with dark wood or leather accents. Engraved or embossed decoration of hibiscus flowers, bamboo, batik-like flowers and rope borders. Cool, bright, refined, with a tropical colonial elegance. Surfaces are clean and tactile, with ornament kept shallow and restrained against large plain areas of polished metal.'),
('Lego','Europe','1970s-present','toys','In the style of Lego, glossy hard plastic building blocks in saturated primary red, blue, yellow and white plus black, grey and green. Everything is a rectangular modular volume with a regular grid of round studs on top, crisp moulded edges and visible seams, so any subject reads as assembled from simple bricks. Characters have cylindrical yellow heads with dot eyes and a simple smile, claw hands and blocky bodies. Packaging uses bold colour fields, dynamic action photos, clean line instruction diagrams, chunky rounded sans-serif lettering and bright playful lighting.'),
('Playmobil','Europe','1970s-present','toys','In the style of Playmobil, small hard plastic figures with oversized round heads, simple dot eyes, a curved smile line, C-shaped hands that grip tiny accessories and stiff jointed limbs on a standardised block body. Bright primary red, yellow, blue and green plus brown and grey in a matte to satin finish. Scenes are built as small dioramas with thin moulded details and clip-on hats and wigs. Packaging has a clear window, yellow and blue graphics, a cheerful rounded logo and soft even lighting.'),
('Hornby','Europe','1930s-60s','toys','In the style of Hornby, nostalgic mid-century British model railway look in tinplate and die-cast metal. Glossy dark green, maroon, black, cream and crimson paint with fine gold lining, polished brass domes and chimney caps, tiny rivets and handrails, and tin buildings with printed brickwork. Boxes are blue or red with a ruled border, a painted illustration of a speeding steam train with white smoke over green countryside, and old-fashioned serif and block capitals. Warm catalogue charm.'),
('Meccano','Europe','1920s-60s','toys','In the style of Meccano, an engineering construction kit look of perforated flat metal strips, girders, plates and wheels with evenly spaced round holes, bolted together with tiny hex nuts and bolts. Red and green enamel or zinc and brass finishes, with brass gears, flanged wheels, handles and cranks. Packaging shows an illustrated scene of a huge model at work in muted red, green and cream, with ornate Edwardian serif lettering, banner panels, line drawings and numbered parts like an engineering manual.'),
('Matchbox','Europe','1950s-60s','toys','In the style of Matchbox, tiny die-cast models with subdued realistic period colours of pastel green, cream, powder blue and brick red, grey wheels, a stamped baseplate, silver painted trim and clear glazing, with soft cast detail and everyday ordinary subjects. Packed in a small yellow and red cardboard box styled like a matchbox, with a line drawing on the end flap and a bold white-on-red numbered label. Modest, collectable and nostalgic.'),
('Hot Wheels','North America','1968-1970s','toys','In the style of Hot Wheels, high-energy speed look with sparkling candy-coloured metallic paint in magenta, aqua, lime, orange and gold. Exaggerated low wide stance, oversized rear wheels with fat slicks, exposed chrome engines, flame and stripe decals and thin red pinstripes. Packaging has a flaming bold italic logo, orange loops, cartoon speed blurs and red, yellow and blue 1970s graphics on a blister card. Loud, glossy, fast and rebellious.'),
('Barbie house style','North America','1960s-present','toys','In the style of Barbie doll playsets, saturated hot pink dominating everything, accented with turquoise, white and lilac. Glossy moulded plastic dream-home furniture, sports cars and campers, miniature fashion accessories, a slim doll with a long ponytail, arched eyebrows and side-glancing painted eyes. Packaging uses a candy pink backdrop, a swirling script logo, sparkles, hearts and clear window panels. Sweet, glamorous and aspirational, with both 1960s retro and modern glam variations.'),
('Mattel','North America','1960s-80s','toys','In the style of Mattel, bright glossy moulded vinyl and plastic in strong primary red, blue and yellow with a hot pink accent. Rounded friendly forms, chunky heroic figures with exaggerated muscles and painted details. Packaging features splashy painted or photographed illustration with starburst flashes, bold block lettering with outline and drop shadow, retro 1970s and 80s cartoon graphics and bubble packs with a header card. Loud, toy-aisle fun.'),
('Fisher-Price','North America','1950s-70s','toys','In the style of Fisher-Price, chunky, rounded, toddler-safe forms in plastic and painted wood with thick rounded corners everywhere. Primary red, blue, yellow and green with white, simple smiling faces made of two dot eyes, rolling wheels with dotted rims, rotating bead handles and round-headed peg figures with simple painted faces. Lithographed labels with simple cartoon animals and rounded sans-serif lettering. Nursery cheerfulness, sturdy mid-century proportions and friendly safety.'),
('Steiff','Europe','1900s-present','toys','In the style of Steiff, soft plush made of mohair, felt or woven fur in honey gold, cream, caramel brown and grey. Shoe-button black eyes, a stitched nose and mouth in dark thread, long jointed limbs, a slight hump on the back, fine stitched seams and wood-wool stuffing. A shiny metal button and tiny tag in the left ear. Realistic proportions, antique worn feel, warm sentimental nursery mood and soft studio lighting.'),
('Ravensburger','Europe','1950s-present','toys','In the style of Ravensburger, sturdy family-game packaging with a blue banner stripe across the top and a small blue triangle mark. Glossy painted illustrations in a detailed, realistic fantasy manner with saturated colour, soft gradients and warm glow, filled with castles, fairs, fairytale landscapes and busy town scenes and cheerful friendly characters. Clean bright cartoon illustration, a bold rounded title face and a playful European family feel.'),
('Schleich','Europe','1980s-present','toys','In the style of Schleich, hand-painted hard rubbery figures with finely sculpted anatomy, realistic proportions and subtle airbrushed shading. Animals in bay, chestnut, grey and black with white socks, fine strand texture in manes and tails, glossy eyes, soft gradient painting on belly and muzzle, a satin matte finish and a small embossed mark underneath. Fantasy creatures follow the same refined realism. Presented on a card with a green nature backdrop.'),
('Bandai','East Asia','1980s-present','toys','In the style of Bandai, crisp, hobby-grade plastic model look with clean panel lines, colour blocking in white, red, blue and yellow, v-shaped chest vents and antenna-like head crests. Mix of glossy and matte plastic with chrome stickers and foil, gold and metallic details, runners of coloured parts on sprues and small decal sheets. Box art shows a dramatic painted pose against fiery explosions and bright starry skies, with clean modern Japanese product graphics in bold and condensed sans-serif lettering.'),
('Tomy','East Asia','1970s-80s','toys','In the style of Tomy, compact, precise Japanese toy design with bright, clean plastic and die-cast metal bodies, glossy red, blue, white and yellow paint, thin black wheels with chrome rims, transforming parts and cute little vehicles on blue plastic track. Packaging uses a bold red or blue header, an illustrated racing scene and cheerful 1970s sans-serif lettering with simple stripes, neat panel graphics and precise small details.'),
('Sanrio','East Asia','1970s-present','characters','In the style of Sanrio, kawaii character cuteness with round simple faces, tiny black dot eyes spaced wide apart, a small oval nose or no mouth, thick uniform soft outlines and big heads on short bodies. Pastel pink, baby blue, lavender, mint and white with a red bow accent. Hearts, stars, strawberries and tiny flowers scatter over gloss sticker finishes, with rounded bubble lettering in cute handwriting, glitter and lots of white space. Sweet candy-coloured gift-shop mood.'),
('Pop Mart','East Asia','2010s-present','toys','In the style of Pop Mart, collectable designer vinyl look with oversized round heads, tiny bodies, large glossy eyes in turquoise or pink and small fanged smiles. Sculpted fur, hoods, wings and crowns, a matte pastel finish in baby blue, mint, peach, lavender and cream, with sharp painted details. Clean glossy colour-block packaging, small logo and a window showing a peeking face. Sweet but quirky, modern urban art-toy mood.'),
('Studio Ghibli','East Asia','1980s-2010s','animation','In the style of Studio Ghibli, hand-painted animation with lush watercolour and gouache backgrounds, towering cumulus clouds in deep blue skies, rolling green meadows, wind in the grass, foggy forests, old stone villages and steam-age machinery with soft rounded edges. Characters have simple faces with small dot-like noses, big expressive eyes and natural proportions, gently flowing hair and clothes in earthy cream, olive, sky blue and warm red. Soft cel shading, warm glowing light, hand-drawn detail, a quiet pastoral and fantastical atmosphere.'),
('Pixar','North America','1995-present','animation','In the style of Pixar, polished 3D computer animation with rounded, squash-and-stretch forms, big expressive eyes and exaggerated but appealing proportions. Soft translucent skin, detailed fur, and convincing plastic, metal and fabric textures. Warm cinematic lighting with strong colour planning, saturated yet harmonious palettes, shallow depth of field and a heartfelt storybook feel. Environments are packed with tiny believable props, glossy reflections and soft shadows with a clean modern family-film finish.'),
('Disney classic','North America','1930s-50s','animation','In the style of Disney classic animation, hand-inked cel characters with rubbery round shapes, bold black outlines, big eyes with highlights and expressive squash-and-stretch poses. Lush painted backgrounds in soft watercolour with storybook castles, deep forests and twinkling night skies. Palette of royal blue, rose pink, golden yellow and emerald with pastel gradients, layered depth, dreamy glowing light, ornate curlicue title lettering and warm nostalgic 1940s picture-book charm.'),
('Aardman','Europe','1990s-present','animation','In the style of Aardman, stop-motion clay with visible thumbprint texture, wide mouths full of big teeth, round bulging eyes with tiny pupils, lumpy bodies and plasticine skin in warm earthy tones. Cosy British interiors with patterned wallpaper, chunky cardboard and wood props, small gadgets and contraptions, soft practical lighting and slightly wobbly handmade imperfections. Charming, comic and deadpan. Characters and objects look sculpted by hand, with soft rounded edges, fingerprint marks and playful oversize features.'),
('Laika','North America','2009-present','animation','In the style of Laika, stop-motion puppets with intricately carved faces, delicate printed expressions, stylised angular or spindly bodies and textured knitted and sewn costumes. Atmospheric miniature sets with moody lighting, moss, mist and dark woodland, a slightly eerie and gothic palette of teal, dusty purple, ochre and charcoal with punches of bright colour. Tactile handmade detail down to individual hair, wood grain and fabric weave, with a dreamy fairy-tale spookiness.'),
('Cartoon Network studio style','North America','1990s-2010s','animation','In the style of Cartoon Network original series, flat bold-colour 2D cartoons with thick uniform outlines, geometric simplified characters, huge heads, dot or pie-cut eyes and noodle limbs. Exaggerated reaction faces, graphic backgrounds in solid saturated fields of magenta, teal, lime and orange, retro-futuristic shapes and chunky sans-serif titles with checkerboard or stripe motifs. Clean vector shapes, quirky off-kilter perspective and a loud, irreverent, pop-art look.'),
('Hanna-Barbera','North America','1960s-70s','animation','In the style of Hanna-Barbera, limited-animation TV cartoons with thick brown-black outlines and flat colours with minimal shading. Gaudy mid-century backgrounds painted in loose blobs with a repeating tree, rock and bush. Characters wear a single colour outfit with a matching collar line and have big round noses, with the head separate from the body for easy animation. Saturated orange, turquoise, brown and mustard palette, simple rounded shapes and a cheerful retro Saturday-morning feel.'),
('Warner cartoons','North America','1940s-50s','animation','In the style of Warner Bros classic cartoons, hand-drawn rubbery, loose characters with extreme squash-and-stretch takes, wide toothy grins, white glove hands, long ears and beaks and sharp expressive poses. Stylised painted desert, forest and city backgrounds with flat angular mid-century shapes, bold ink outlines and saturated colour in orange, sky blue, brown and grey. Concentric-ring title cards with a red and gold shield look and a zippy, irreverent slapstick attitude.'),
('Toei Animation','East Asia','1960s-80s','animation','In the style of Toei Animation, cel animation with bold clean outlines, expressive heroes with tall spiky hair, huge shiny eyes with highlights, angular muscular poses and dramatic speed lines. Painted backgrounds with vivid sunset skies and mechanical interiors, flashy energy blasts in cyan, magenta and yellow, bold colour coding for teams of heroes, and princess characters with long flowing hair and stars sparkling in the eyes. Rich classic 1970s TV anime look.'),
('Gainax','East Asia','1990s-2000s','animation','In the style of Gainax, anime with angular, sharp-chinned characters, thin lines, sleek armoured mecha, stark black title cards in heavy serif type on plain colour, glowing orange and violet sunsets, silhouetted skylines and wires. Nervous close-ups on eyes, bold high-contrast colour fields in red, purple, white and teal, hot-blooded exaggerated poses with extreme foreshortening, and a mix of gritty realism and flamboyant over-the-top energy.'),
('Kyoto Animation','East Asia','2000s-10s','animation','In the style of Kyoto Animation, exquisitely polished anime with soft pastel palettes, big luminous eyes with detailed iris gradients, delicate hair strands catching light, and everyday settings drawn with careful realism. Bokeh lens flares, gentle depth of field, cherry blossoms and glowing golden hour light. Smooth fluid motion, rounded cute faces with tiny blush marks, and a warm slice-of-life mood with luminous airy backgrounds.'),
('Soyuzmultfilm','Russia and Eastern Europe','1950s-80s','animation','In the style of Soyuzmultfilm, Soviet-era hand-drawn and cut-out animation with soft gouache backgrounds in muted greens, earthy browns, dusty blue and warm ochre. Folk-tale forests, wooden huts and snowy villages, characters with round gentle faces, big noses and woolly fur textures, quirky puppet-like proportions, painterly grainy textures, simple slightly naive shapes and hand-lettered titles with a red star. Warm, melancholic, slightly surreal fairy-tale feel.'),
('Zagreb animation school','Russia and Eastern Europe','1960s-70s','animation','In the style of the Zagreb school of animation, modernist flat 2D cartoons with minimal geometric characters made of simple shapes, thin line work, little or no shading and large blank backgrounds in single flat colours. Witty visual metaphors, angular stylised figures with stick-like limbs, abstract pop-art colour blocks in red, yellow, black and sky blue, jazzy off-balance compositions and a sophisticated deadpan, urbane 1960s graphic-design look.'),
('Archie Comics','North America','1950s-70s','comics','In the style of Archie Comics, wholesome teenage newsstand comics with clean, uniform thin black outlines, simple friendly characters with round heads, dot eyes, button noses, bright wide grins and neat hairstyles. Flat saturated four-colour printing with halftone dots on slightly yellowed pulp paper in red, yellow, blue and green, sock-hop and soda-shop settings, speech balloons in a hand-lettered rounded face and a cheerful clean-cut mid-century small-town mood.'),
('Marvel Silver Age','North America','1960s','comics','In the style of Marvel Silver Age comics, dynamic muscular heroes with dramatic foreshortening, bold black ink with heavy shadows and halftone dots in four-colour print. Primary red, blue and yellow with purple and green accents, fists bursting out of the panel, cosmic energy crackles, cheerful yellow caption boxes, bold all-caps hand-lettered balloons with exclamation points, jagged starburst sound effects and a mighty cover logo box in the top left corner.'),
('DC Golden Age','North America','1930s-40s','comics','In the style of DC Golden Age comics, muscular flat-coloured heroes in tight capes and trunks over bold chest symbols, stiff but powerful poses, bold black ink outlines and simple shading. Limited four-colour palette of red, blue, yellow and green with coarse halftone dots on yellowing newsprint, city skylines with art deco towers, dramatic cover scenes of villains and lurid rays, wartime patriotic motifs, bold stacked masthead lettering and a naive pulp-adventure energy.'),
('2000 AD','Europe','1977-1990s','comics','In the style of 2000 AD, British sci-fi comics with gritty, hyper-detailed pen and ink, dystopian megacities of towering tenements and neon, helmeted enforcers in spiked armour, robots and aliens. Painted covers with metallic airbrush gloss in lurid red, green and electric blue, black-and-white interiors with dense hatching, jagged sound effects, a bold angular logo and a loud, punky, sardonic and violent futuristic attitude.'),
('Tintin studio','Europe','1930s-70s','comics','In the style of the Belgian Tintin studio, the clear line school of comics with uniform thin black outlines, flat cheerful fills and no hatching. Meticulously accurate backgrounds drawn with research and care, characters with round simple faces, dot eyes and an upswept tuft of hair, a limited palette of sea blue, sand yellow, warm red and green, stage-like panel compositions, tidy hand-lettered balloons and the glossy hardcover album format with a flat colour spine.'),
('Shueisha Jump','East Asia','1980s-present','comics','In the style of Shueisha Jump magazine manga, black and white pages with dynamic action lines, bold inked outlines and screentone shading. Spiky-haired muscular heroes, enormous eyes, exaggerated expressions, huge sound effects in brush-like lettering, dramatic speed-line backgrounds, colour covers in neon orange, cyan and yellow with a starburst title banner, tightly packed panels and a hot-blooded, high-energy weekly adventure look.'),
('Penguin Books','Europe','1930s-60s','publishing','In the style of Penguin Books paperbacks, a rigorous three-band cover layout with a central white panel framed by two coloured stripes, orange for fiction, green for crime and blue for non-fiction. Title and author are set in clean sans-serif or classic serif inside the white band, with a small bird logo at the bottom. Later covers use a Swiss-style grid with bold illustration. Mid-century uncoated paper, matte printing and crisp rules.'),
('Taschen','Europe','1990s-present','publishing','In the style of Taschen art books, oversized heavy hardcover coffee-table volumes with glossy photo or painting covers bleeding edge to edge, a plain contrasting colour bar or foil-stamped title and rich saturated reproduction. Large crisp images on thick paper, stylish clean sans-serif titles, hefty slipcase boxes with a satin finish and a bold, sensual, curious art and pop-culture look.'),
('Blue Note Records','North America','1950s-60s','music','In the style of Blue Note Records album covers, bold modernist graphic design with tightly cropped monochrome or duotone photography in blue, black and white. Large asymmetrical heavy sans-serif type in unexpected angled lines, slabs of solid colour in orange, red or cyan cutting across the image, tilted and overprinted lettering, thin rules and grainy high-contrast portraits. Cool, smoky, mid-century jazz club feel.'),
('Factory Records','Europe','1979-1980s','music','In the style of Factory Records sleeve design, cool, austere post-punk minimalism with large empty space and thin sans-serif type. Coded barcode-like or abstract geometric patterns, industrial hazard stripes in black and yellow, silver or metallic ink on matt grey stock, die-cut and textured cardboard, muted greys, steel blues and muted pastel colours, grainy halftone photographs and a clinical, enigmatic, modernist attitude.'),
('Saul Bass era title houses','North America','1950s-60s','film graphics','In the style of Saul Bass era title houses, bold flat cut-paper graphics with jagged torn black shapes and white or red hand-cut lettering. Angular silhouettes, arrows and stark symbols, a limited palette of black, white, orange and red, stylised spirals, kinetic typography that slides and spins, rough-edged textures and one simple powerful symbol per composition. Graphic, sharp, tense and modernist.'),
('Hammer Films','Europe','1950s-70s','film','In the style of Hammer Films gothic horror, richly saturated colour in blood red, deep green and midnight blue. Candle-lit castles, fog-wrapped graveyards and crypts, ornate Victorian costumes and capes, fangs, dripping crimson blood, dramatic painted posters with screaming women and looming shadows, lurid yellow and red title lettering with jagged dripping edges and studio-built sets with painted skies. Lush, lurid storybook creepiness.'),
('Amblin','North America','1980s','film','In the style of Amblin Entertainment films, suburban childhood adventure in the 1980s with kids on bicycles silhouetted against a huge glowing moon, warm backlit mist and lens flares, golden-hour streetlight beams, flashlights in dark woods and wonder-struck faces lit from below. Painted posters with soft airbrushed glow in deep blue and orange, wide-eyed friendly creatures and a warm nostalgic magic-hour glow.'),
('A24','North America','2010s-present','film','In the style of A24 films and posters, minimalist, offbeat design with a clean sans-serif or serif title in white on a muted or saturated single colour, a stark centred or off-balance photograph, soft grainy film texture and pastel or sun-bleached colour or deep moody darkness. Symmetrical compositions, wide-angle lenses, naturalistic light, surreal touches and an arthouse, intimate, slightly uncanny indie look.'),
]
